## Time Complexity

The algorithm contains three nested loops:

```text
V × V × V
```

Therefore:

```text
O(V³)
```

---

## Space Complexity

Distance matrix:

```text
V × V
```

Therefore:

```text
O(V²)
```

---

## Negative Cycle Detection

A unique advantage of Floyd Warshall is detecting negative cycles.

After the algorithm:

```cpp
if(dist[i][i] < 0)
```

then a negative-weight cycle exists.

Reason:

A node should never have a negative distance to itself unless a negative cycle is present.

---

## Floyd Warshall vs Dijkstra vs Bellman Ford

| Algorithm | Source | Negative Edges | All Pairs |
|------------|---------|---------------|-----------|
| Dijkstra | Single Source | ❌ No | ❌ |
| Bellman Ford | Single Source | ✅ Yes | ❌ |
| Floyd Warshall | All Sources | ✅ Yes | ✅ |

---

## Key Learning

- Floyd Warshall solves the All-Pairs Shortest Path problem.
- Uses Dynamic Programming instead of Greedy techniques.
- Works with both positive and negative edge weights.
- Can detect negative cycles.
- One of the most important graph algorithms for interview preparation.

